data: {"type":"response.reasoning_summary_text.done","sequence_number":81,"item_id":"rs_012c83c1bcd0e5ac016acab153c708819597e7c3e7340b4ffa","output_index":0,"summary_index":0,"text":"**Considering test file management**\n\nI’m thinking about how to add tests via bash efficiently. It seems like I might prefer creating new test files instead of editing existing ones, especially for migration tests. By duplicating helpers, I could streamline the process without risking any issues while trying to append to existing files. Okay, I need to figure out the best approach for writing these tests and keeping everything organized during the migration."}

